229 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/ActualText ( Through the consistency in our programing presets many kids were able to drive the bot and have a great time interacting with the team. When we were working with the kids at the First Lego League competition, we were able to discuss a lot about our bot and what we had to accomplish in the game. This included picking up pixels and placing them on the backdrop, hanging on scaffolding, and launching an airplane.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
230 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 134 0 R
/ActualText (   Many curious parents and children came to us asking questions about our robot, as well as to ask us if they could try driving our bot. Kids and their parents were learning about CAD, our bot, and FIRST Tech Challenge.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
