251 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/ActualText (   CAD or Computer Aided Design has helped our team a lot this year. CAD is a software used for modeling 3D parts and designs. These designs act like a 3D blueprint that is then followed or printed. The use of CAD software like Onshape has allowed our team to take a step forward on all designs with the ability to suit our parts exactly to our needs.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
252 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/ActualText (     One example of this is our gear box, which holds the claw and allows us to align to the floor for accurate pixel pickup. Through various iterations we were able to improve tensile and compressive strength along with minimizing the weight suspended on our lift arm and wrist joint.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/ActualText (   The original design of this gear box was built from goBILDA parts, specifically a servo mount connected to a 2-hole shallow U-channel with a 1-hole U-channel. This design proved too heavy for our wrist servo, which led to the burning out of several servos at meet 1. We had to come up with a solution.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
254 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 136 0 R
/ActualText (   The design to the left is the first CAD model of the gear box that was designed and outfitted to the bot, lowering the weight and further enabling further dexterity to the claw.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
