/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/ActualText (    With the addition of our new hanging system and additional drivers practice, we could now consistently grab 2 pixels and place them simultaneously on the board with more precision, a shift in strategy which opened up more opportunities for points.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
310 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 140 0 R
/ActualText (    We would grab 2 pixels at a time, placing all the pixels to one side of the board, aiming to get them above the first scoring line for the points bonus. Once in end- game we would aim to score 1-2 more times on the board and with ~10 seconds left we would attempt to hang. We did notice that when attempting the hang it would sometimes fail due to the gears used becoming misaligned. However, we later fix that issue.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [14]
>>
endobj
