/P 144 0 R
/T (This year, we took a more organized approach to the code of the systems on the robot. Instead of defining them all in one place, we made them all different subsystems. Each subsystem consists of an interface and a class. Methods are made and the subsystem is privately initialized and made part of the hardware map. After that programmers can make that subsystem accessible from whichever class you like!)
/E (This year, we took a more organized approach to the code of the systems on the robot. Instead of defining them all in one place, we made them all different subsystems. Each subsystem consists of an interface and a class. Methods are made and the subsystem is privately initialized and made part of the hardware map. After that programmers can make that subsystem accessible from whichever class you like!)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [12]
>>
